<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM Q3 revenues and costs in detail.</title>
<headline>KLM Q3 revenues and costs in detail.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q3 1996/97 to Dec 31 1996.</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>OPERATING REVENUES</p>
<p>    KLM passenger traffic (billions)    1.66  vs    1.51</p>
<p>    KLM cargo traffic		     470     vs  450</p>
<p>Traffic revenues of other</p>
<p>    consolidated companies		 92     vs  101</p>
<p>    Other revenue			   328     vs  296</p>
<p>    TOTAL REVENUES (billions)	     2.55  vs    2.35</p>
<p>OPERATING COSTS</p>
<p>    Salaries/benefits		     742     vs  669</p>
<p>    Aircraft fuel			   292     vs  209</p>
<p>    Materials/consumables		 159     vs  148</p>
<p>    Commercial costs			246     vs  249</p>
<p>    Landing/navigation charges	  207     vs  185</p>
<p>    Third-party handling costs	   83     vs   72</p>
<p>    Work by third parties		 196     vs  176</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    209     vs  213</p>
<p>    Operational lease expenses	   48     vs   23</p>
<p>    Miscellaneous			   383     vs  353</p>
<p>    TOTAL OPERATING COSTS (billions)    2.57  vs    2.30</p>
<p>NOTES - KLM said the 11 percent increase in salaries and benefits broke down as follows: increase in number of employees (six pct); resumption of pension contributions by the company (one pct); rise in average wage costs per employee (four pct).</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
